error[ffi_not_constant]: `fixedbugs-2333-checks.h` has `HERO_2333_OUT`, but not as a constant — clang cannot read its value while compiling
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2333-a-group-header-s-constant-p-macro-leaves-an-object-refused.hero:9:5
    |
  9 |     constant HERO_2333_OUT: ptr  #~ ffi_not_constant
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: a `constant` names one value forever (§4.4), and clang reads `HERO_2333_OUT` as something computed each time it is read, an object, a call or a statement expression it does not fold, so nothing holds two reads of it to one answer: the mutable global §4.2 forbids. A value computed in C is reached through a function of the program's own that returns it, written in a header beside this file and bound by `extern` naming that header like any function: `static inline <its C type> hero_HERO_2333_OUT(void) { return HERO_2333_OUT; }`
